# Windows Server Infrastructure Lab – IIS, SQL Server, AD Authorization, and File Backups

## 1. Overview

This lab focused on building and validating a Windows Server infrastructure environment using Active Directory, IIS, ASP.NET Core, SQL Server Express, and SMB file sharing.

The main goal was to practice role-based access control, web application deployment, database integration, and backup operations while keeping the Production and Staging environments separate.

## 2. Environment

| Component | Configuration |
|---|---|
| Domain | `DEV.LOCAL` |
| Domain Controller | `DC01` |
| Web and SQL Server | `SQL01` |
| Client machine | `DEV01` |
| Web server | IIS |
| Application | ASP.NET Core EmployeeWeb |
| Database server | SQL Server Express |
| SQL instance | `SQL01\SQLEXPRESS` |
| Production database | `WebAppDB` |
| Staging database | `WebAppDB_Staging` |
